Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.50,0:00:04.29,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}I'm [Name];\NI led modelling and conclusions.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.29,0:00:07.26,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Last question:\Ndoes systematic preparation pay?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.26,0:00:09.80,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Same model, minimal against systematic:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.80,0:00:14.99,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}AUC rises by 0.008,\Ninterval 0.000 to 0.016.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.44,0:00:20.45,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Our smallest effect of interest,\Nfixed in advance, was 0.01.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.45,0:00:23.21,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}The interval covers both no gain\Nand a worthwhile one,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.21,0:00:27.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}so the result is inconclusive:\Nunderpowered, not evidence of no effect.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.30,0:00:29.51,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}One step did harm.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.51,0:00:34.04,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}From minimal to systematic,\Nthe Brier score worsens by 0.074.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.29,0:00:37.00,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}The cause is [Name]'s class weights:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.00,0:00:41.23,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}the systematic model predicts\Nan average risk of 41 percent
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.23,0:00:43.85,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}where the observed rate is 17.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.85,0:00:46.87,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Removing only the class weights\Nrestores calibration
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.87,0:00:50.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}and leaves AUC 0.007 above minimal.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.50,0:00:56.95,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Who does the score serve? On all adults,\Nthe systematic model scores 0.836;
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.95,0:00:59.38,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}on adults not yet diagnosed, 0.781.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.83,0:01:03.93,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}84 percent of positives\Nwere already diagnosed,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.93,0:01:07.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}so the all-adults AUC mostly\Nmeasures recognition: spectrum bias.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.30,0:01:12.03,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Next, drop two items\Nthat mark earlier contact with a doctor.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.03,0:01:15.56,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}On all adults, AUC falls by 0.016.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.56,0:01:17.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}On adults not yet diagnosed,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.40,0:01:22.95,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}it rises by 0.019,\Ninterval 0.004 to 0.034:
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.95,0:01:26.28,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}consistent with recognition\Nand screening pulling apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.53,0:01:31.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}But the lower end lies inside our margin,\Nso it is inconclusive.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.30,0:01:36.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}An internal hold-out of 1,146 adults,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.20,0:01:40.68,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}scored once, repeats the leakage drop\Nand the inconclusive preparation result.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.68,0:01:41.98,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}So, three answers.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.98,0:01:44.19,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}The label records care as well as disease.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.24,0:01:47.42,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}The 0.961 was leakage, not skill.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.47,0:01:53.26,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Systematic preparation barely moved AUC;\Nits value was valid data kept
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.26,0:01:56.10,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}and an honest test\Non adults not yet diagnosed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.30,0:01:59.03,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Most unexpected for me:
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.03,0:02:02.90,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}leakage moved the score far more\Nthan careful preparation did.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.30,0:02:05.99,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Four roles, one audit:
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.99,0:02:10.97,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}[Name]'s governance, [Name]'s preparation,\N[Name]'s labels and bias, my models.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.97,0:02:13.64,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Limits: one survey cycle, low response,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.64,0:02:17.65,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}and only 152 undiagnosed positives;
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.65,0:02:20.68,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}this is a data audit,\Nnot a screening tool.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.68,0:02:23.88,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Generative AI drafted\Nmuch of our code and text;
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.88,0:02:27.13,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}we reviewed it\Nand recomputed every number.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.38,0:02:32.59,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}The score is not the finding;\Nwhat it reveals about the data is.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.59,0:02:33.59,Caption,,0,0,0,,{\fad(100,100)}Thank you.
